  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Inverse"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "$A$ is singular if $|A| = 0$ and non-singular otherwise. A square matrix is invertible if and only if it is non-singular, and then $A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\text{adj}\\,A$. Also $|AB| = |A||B|$ and $|A^{-1}| = 1/|A|$.",
    "kn": "|A| = 0 ಆದರೆ A ಏಕವಚನ (singular). |A| ≠ 0 ಆದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ A ವಿಲೋಮೀಯ, ಮತ್ತು A⁻¹ = adj A / |A|."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "A⁻¹ exists ⇔ |A| ≠ 0"
    },
    {
     "en": "A⁻¹ = adj A / |A|"
    },
    {
     "en": "|AB| = |A||B|"
    },
    {
     "en": "|A⁻¹| = 1/|A|"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "A matrix is invertible exactly when its determinant is not zero. Then the inverse is the adjoint divided by the determinant.",
    "kn": "|A| = 0 ಆದರೆ A ಏಕವಚನ (singular). |A| ≠ 0 ಆದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ A ವಿಲೋಮೀಯ, ಮತ್ತು A⁻¹ = adj A / |A|."
   },
   "formula": "A^{-1} = \\frac{1}{|A|}\\operatorname{adj} A"
  },
  {
   "id": "int1",
   "type": "interactive",
   "title": {
    "en": "Determinant rules for n × n"
   },
   "kind": "readouts",
   "caption": {
    "en": "Set the order n, the determinant |A| and a scalar k. Read the determinants of kA, adj A, A⁻¹ and adj(adj A)."
   },
   "sliders": [
    {
     "name": "n",
     "label": {
      "en": "order n"
     },
     "min": 2,
     "max": 4,
     "step": 1,
     "value": 3
    },
    {
     "name": "d",
     "label": {
      "en": "|A|"
     },
     "min": -5,
     "max": 5,
     "step": 1,
     "value": 4
    },
    {
     "name": "k",
     "label": {
      "en": "k"
     },
     "min": -3,
     "max": 3,
     "step": 1,
     "value": 2
    }
   ],
   "readouts": [
    {
     "label": {
      "en": "|kA| = kⁿ|A|"
     },
     "expr": "k^n*d",
     "digits": 0
    },
    {
     "label": {
      "en": "|adj A| = |A|ⁿ⁻¹"
     },
     "expr": "d^(n - 1)",
     "digits": 0
    },
    {
     "label": {
      "en": "|A⁻¹| = 1/|A|"
     },
     "expr": "1/d",
     "digits": 3
    },
    {
     "label": {
      "en": "|adj(adj A)| = |A|^((n−1)²)"
     },
     "expr": "d^((n - 1)^2)",
     "digits": 0
    }
   ],
   "tryThis": [
    {
     "en": "n = 3, |A| = 4: check |adj A| = 16."
    },
    {
     "en": "Set |A| = 0. Which read-outs break, and why?"
    },
    {
     "en": "Set k = −1 and n = 3. Why is |−A| = −|A|?"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "Move n, the determinant and k. Scaling multiplies the determinant by k to the power n; the adjoint raises it to the power n minus 1."
   },
   "seconds": 120,
   "optional": true
  },
